Measurement uncertainty in conformity assessment — JCGM 106 (@met-decision: 0, is #book, #part-of @met-sources) { r_0VFKYJZJC8BXM2T2TSY58DD6SY
JCGM 106:2012. Evaluation of measurement data — The role of measurement uncertainty in conformity assessment. [Official edition DOI](https://doi.org/10.59161/JCGM106-2012) · [Catalogue](https://www.bipm.org/en/committees/jc/jcgm/publications).

Read the full guide in the conformity and risk study, including the distinction between tolerance and acceptance intervals, decision rules, and risks. Work its examples and compare the conditions behind a probability statement. A generic numerical illustration here is not a replacement for the rule agreed for an actual product or regulated measurement.

The earlier tolerance and uncertainty Records supply the vocabulary; this document supplies a sustained mathematical treatment. Return to its probability definitions when distinguishing a risk for one observed result from a population-averaged risk.

JCGM retains copyright and publication terms despite free access. Identity, contents, and authorized availability checked on 28 October 2026. Reference only; no PDF is bundled.

**Return:** [Measurement and metrology sources — books, guides, and research](../Sources.lingua#r_6H584EJ2Z9D11PG89Y21Y8T1A3).
